'''''Exsertotheca crispa''''', '''crisped neckera''', is a species of [[moss]] belonging to the family [[Neckeraceae]].<ref name="GBIF">{{cite web |title=Exsertotheca crispa (Hedw.) S.Olsson, Enroth & D.Quandt |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/7470937 |website=www.gbif.org |access-date=26 November 2025 |language=en}}</ref>

It is native to Europe and China. In [[Iceland]], it is found at only two locations, growing on [[palagonite]] cliffs, and has the conservation status of a [[vulnerable species]] (VU).<ref Name="NÍ1996">Náttúrufræðistofnun Íslands [Icelandic Institute of Natural History] (1996). ''[http://utgafa.ni.is/valistar/valisti_1.pdf Válisti 1: Plöntur.]'' (in Icelandic) Reykjavík: Náttúrufræðistofnun Íslands.</ref>

